public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }
    while (n > 1) {
        if (n % 3 != 0) {
            return false;
        }
        n = n / 3;
    }
    return true;
}
```

This solution works by repeatedly dividing `n` by 3 until `n` is less than 3. If at any point `n` is not divisible by 3, the function immediately returns `false`, indicating that `n` is not a power of three. If the loop completes without returning, it means `n` is a power of three, and the function returns `true`.

The time complexity of this solution is O(log n), as each iteration divides the number by 3. The space complexity is O(1), as it uses a constant amount of extra space.

